IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `colc-common`
IMPORT `colc-vehicles`

-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website (State of South Australia, CC BY 4.0), taken
-- from the Open Australian Legal Corpus (CC BY 4.0); each text may be out of date.
--
-- Cases for colc-vehicles.l4: the Motor Vehicles Act 1959 and Regulations 2010. Every expected value is worked by hand
-- from the deposited text, with the arithmetic in the comment above the assertion. Prescribed registration fees are
-- ILLUSTRATIVE (the fee scales are not encoded). Clock for the regulative rules: days.

§ `Cases -- the car, the trailer and the driver's licence`

§§ `Builder`

-- Arguments: heavy vehicle; pensioner entitlement card with reduced fares; ex-service member; result of service; lost
-- the use of the legs; parent of such a child; used for the owner; used for the child; another vehicle under the same
-- section; reduced fee under another provision.
GIVEN `heavy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `card` IS A BOOLEAN
      `ex-service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `result` IS A `Result of service`
      `legs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `parent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for the owner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for the child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Motor vehicle and owner`
`a vehicle` `heavy` `card` `ex-service` `result` `legs` `parent` `for the owner` `for the child` `another vehicle` `another provision` MEANS
    `Motor vehicle and owner` WITH
        `the vehicle is a heavy vehicle` IS `heavy`
        `the owner is entitled, as the holder of a Commonwealth pensioner entitlement card, to reduced public transport fares in this State` IS `card`
        `the owner has been a member of a naval, military or air force of Her Majesty` IS `ex-service`
        `as a result of that service the owner` IS `result`
        `the owner, from the loss of the use of 1 or both legs, is permanently unable to use public transport` IS `legs`
        `the owner is the parent or legal guardian of a child who, from the loss of the use of 1 or both legs, is permanently unable to use public transport` IS `parent`
        `the vehicle will be wholly or mainly used for the transport of the owner` IS `for the owner`
        `the vehicle will be wholly or mainly used for transporting the child` IS `for the child`
        `another motor vehicle of the owner is already registered at a reduced fee under the same section` IS `another vehicle`
        `a reduced fee is payable for the vehicle under a provision of the Act other than sections 38 to 38B` IS `another provision`

`no service` MEANS `none of these, or no such service`

-- Margaret: Pensioner Concession Card, reduced fares, drives herself.
`Margaret's car` MEANS `a vehicle` FALSE TRUE FALSE `no service` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Walter: ex-RAAF, totally and permanently incapacitated by service, no pensioner card.
`Walter's car` MEANS `a vehicle` FALSE FALSE TRUE `totally and permanently incapacitated` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE

§§ `ss 37A, 38, 38A, 38B -- which reduction`

-- s 38A(1).
#ASSERT `the registration concession for the vehicle` `Margaret's car` EQUALS `section 38A: the registration fee reduced by 50%`
-- s 38(1).
#ASSERT `the registration concession for the vehicle` `Walter's car` EQUALS `section 38: the registration fee reduced by 66.667%`
-- s 38(1)(b): blindness from service counts for registration ...
#ASSERT `the registration concession for the vehicle` (`a vehicle` FALSE FALSE TRUE `blind` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `section 38: the registration fee reduced by 66.667%`
-- ... but "totally or permanently" (not both) does not (finding 17).
#ASSERT `the registration concession for the vehicle` (`a vehicle` FALSE FALSE TRUE `incapacitated totally or permanently, but not both` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `no reduction under sections 38 to 38B` `the conditions of sections 38, 38A and 38B are not met`
-- s 38(1)(a): the result of service without having been a member does not count.
#ASSERT `the registration concession for the vehicle` (`a vehicle` FALSE FALSE FALSE `totally and permanently incapacitated` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `no reduction under sections 38 to 38B` `the conditions of sections 38, 38A and 38B are not met`
-- s 38B(1)(a): an owner who has lost the use of the legs.
#ASSERT `the registration concession for the vehicle` (`a vehicle` FALSE FALSE FALSE `no service` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `section 38B: the registration fee reduced by 50%`
-- s 38B(1)(b): the parent of such a child, the car used mainly to take the child.
#ASSERT `the registration concession for the vehicle` (`a vehicle` FALSE FALSE FALSE `no service` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `section 38B: the registration fee reduced by 50%`
-- s 37A: never for a heavy vehicle.
#ASSERT `the registration concession for the vehicle` (`a vehicle` TRUE TRUE FALSE `no service` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `no reduction under sections 38 to 38B` `the vehicle is a heavy vehicle (section 37A)`
-- s 38A(1)(b): a pensioner's car used mainly by her son is not reduced.
#ASSERT `the registration concession for the vehicle` (`a vehicle` FALSE TRUE FALSE `no service` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `no reduction under sections 38 to 38B` `the conditions of sections 38, 38A and 38B are not met`
-- s 38A(2)(a): only one vehicle per owner.
#ASSERT `the registration concession for the vehicle` (`a vehicle` FALSE TRUE FALSE `no service` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `no reduction under sections 38 to 38B` `another of my vehicles already has the reduced fee under that section (subsection (2)(a))`
-- s 38A(2)(b): a car already reduced under s 37 (outer areas) is not reduced again.
#ASSERT `the registration concession for the vehicle` (`a vehicle` FALSE TRUE FALSE `no service` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `no reduction under sections 38 to 38B` `a reduced fee is payable under another provision of the Act (subsection (2)(b))`
-- An ex-service pensioner meets both s 38 and s 38A; each excludes the other (finding 16).
#ASSERT `the registration concession for the vehicle` (`a vehicle` FALSE TRUE TRUE `totally and permanently incapacitated` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `not covered: more than one of sections 38, 38A and 38B would apply, and each excludes a vehicle with a reduced fee under another of them`

§§ `reg 77(3), (4) -- the fee`

-- reg 77(4): $400 less 50% of $400 = $200.
#ASSERT `the registration fee after the reduction` `section 38A: the registration fee reduced by 50%` 400 EQUALS 200
-- reg 77(3): $300 less 66.667% of $300 (200.001) = 99.999 (no rounding is stated).
#ASSERT `the registration fee after the reduction` `section 38: the registration fee reduced by 66.667%` 300 EQUALS 99.999
#ASSERT `the registration fee after the reduction` (`no reduction under sections 38 to 38B` `the conditions of sections 38, 38A and 38B are not met`) 400 EQUALS 400

§§ `s 38AB -- the trailer`

GIVEN `heavy` IS A BOOLEAN, `card` IS A BOOLEAN, `personal use` IS A BOOLEAN, `another trailer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Trailer and owner`
`a trailer` `heavy` `card` `personal use` `another trailer` MEANS
    `Trailer and owner` WITH
        `the trailer is a heavy vehicle` IS `heavy`
        `the owner is entitled, as the holder of a Commonwealth pensioner entitlement card, to reduced public transport fares in this State` IS `card`
        `the trailer will be wholly or mainly employed in the personal use of the owner` IS `personal use`
        `another trailer of the owner is already registered at a reduced fee under section 38AB` IS `another trailer`

-- s 38AB(1), reg 77(4): $100 less 50% = $50.
#ASSERT `the trailer's registration fee after the reduction` (`a trailer` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE) 100 EQUALS 50
-- s 38AB(2): a second trailer pays the full $100.
#ASSERT `the trailer's registration fee after the reduction` (`a trailer` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE) 100 EQUALS 100
-- s 38AB(1)(b): a trailer used mainly for a business pays the full fee.
#ASSERT `the trailer's registration fee after the reduction` (`a trailer` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) 100 EQUALS 100

§§ `ss 38A(3), 40, 40A -- death, sale, the balance, refunds`

#ASSERT `subsection (3) applies to the event` `the registered owner dies`
#ASSERT `subsection (3) applies to the event` `the registered owner ceases to be the owner of the vehicle`
-- Losing the card while keeping the car does not end the reduced registration (finding 18).
#ASSERT NOT (`subsection (3) applies to the event` `the owner stops holding the card or ceases to meet the conditions, still owning the vehicle`)
-- Death on 31 January 2025: one month runs to 28 February 2025.
#ASSERT DATE_SERIAL (`the day the reduced-fee registration becomes void unless the balance is paid` (YMD 2025 1 31)) EQUALS DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2025 2 28)
-- Sale on 10 March 2025: to 10 April 2025.
#ASSERT DATE_SERIAL (`the day the reduced-fee registration becomes void unless the balance is paid` (YMD 2025 3 10)) EQUALS DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2025 4 10)
-- s 40: $400 less the $200 paid.
#ASSERT `the balance of the prescribed registration fee` 400 200 EQUALS 200
-- s 40A.
#ASSERT `the section 40A refund` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the Registrar may refund such part of the registration fee as the Registrar thinks just`
#ASSERT `the section 40A refund` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no refund under section 40A`
#ASSERT `the section 40A refund` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no refund under section 40A`

§§ `Schedule 1 clause 22 -- the driver's licence`

GIVEN `result` IS A `Result of service`, `card` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Licence applicant`
`an applicant` `result` `card` MEANS
    `Licence applicant` WITH
        `as a result of service in a naval, military or air force of His Majesty the applicant` IS `result`
        `the applicant is a pensioner entitlement card holder` IS `card`

-- cl 22(1)(b): $26 a year; ten years (40 complete 3-month periods) x $26 / 4 = $260.
#ASSERT `the driver's licence fee for the period` (`an applicant` `no service` TRUE) 120 EQUALS 260
#ASSERT `the driver's licence fee for the period` (`an applicant` `no service` TRUE) 12 EQUALS 26
-- cl 22(2): 18 months is 6 quarters: 6 x 6.50 = 39; 20 months is still 6 complete quarters: 39.
#ASSERT `the driver's licence fee for the period` (`an applicant` `no service` TRUE) 18 EQUALS 39
#ASSERT `the driver's licence fee for the period` (`an applicant` `no service` TRUE) 20 EQUALS 39
-- cl 22(1)(c): $53 a year; ten years 40 x 13.25 = 530.
#ASSERT `the driver's licence fee for the period` (`an applicant` `no service` FALSE) 120 EQUALS 530
#ASSERT `the driver's licence fee for the period` (`an applicant` `no service` FALSE) 12 EQUALS 53
-- cl 22(1)(a)(i): "totally or permanently" incapacitated by service, no card: $26.
#ASSERT `the driver's licence fee for the period` (`an applicant` `incapacitated totally or permanently, but not both` FALSE) 12 EQUALS 26
-- cl 22(1)(a) has no "blind" limb: blind from service, no card: $53 (finding 17).
#ASSERT `the driver's licence fee for the period` (`an applicant` `blind` FALSE) 12 EQUALS 53
-- cl 22(5), cl 1: level 2 fee, $20.
#ASSERT `the administration fee for the issue or renewal of a driver's licence` EQUALS 20

-- cl 22(3), (4): ceased 15 March 2025; licence expires 14 March 2030: 60 complete months, 20 quarters;
-- 20 x (53 - 26) / 4 = 20 x 6.75 = 135.
#ASSERT `the complete 3 month periods in the unexpired period of the licence` (YMD 2025 3 15) (YMD 2030 3 14) EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `the additional licence fee on ceasing to be a card holder` (`an applicant` `no service` FALSE) TRUE (YMD 2025 3 15) (YMD 2030 3 14) EQUALS 135
-- Ceased 15 March 2025; licence expires 31 August 2025: 15 March to 14 June is one complete 3 months; the next would end
-- 14 September, after expiry: 1 quarter, 6.75.
#ASSERT `the additional licence fee on ceasing to be a card holder` (`an applicant` `no service` FALSE) TRUE (YMD 2025 3 15) (YMD 2025 8 31) EQUALS 6.75
-- An eligible ex-service holder would pay $26 anyway: nothing extra.
#ASSERT `the additional licence fee on ceasing to be a card holder` (`an applicant` `has lost a leg or foot` FALSE) TRUE (YMD 2025 3 15) (YMD 2030 3 14) EQUALS 0
-- Licence taken at the full fee: nothing extra.
#ASSERT `the additional licence fee on ceasing to be a card holder` (`an applicant` `no service` FALSE) FALSE (YMD 2025 3 15) (YMD 2030 3 14) EQUALS 0
-- reg 76(4).
#ASSERT `the Registrar's notice allows enough time` 14
#ASSERT NOT (`the Registrar's notice allows enough time` 10)

§§ `Regulative rules`

-- s 38A(3): death on 31 January 2025: 28 days to 28 February. The balance of $200 is paid on day 20.
#ASSERT `days from` (YMD 2025 1 31) `to` (`one month after` (YMD 2025 1 31)) EQUALS 28
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 38A(3) -- after death or sale, pay the balance within one month or the registration is void` 200 28) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the registered owner or operator` (`pay the Registrar the balance of the prescribed registration fee` 200) 20)) EQUALS FULFILLED

#TRACE `s 38A(3) -- after death or sale, pay the balance within one month or the registration is void` 200 28 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 29)
-- expect: the registration is void; a prohibition remains: PARTY `a person driving the vehicle` MUST NOT `drive the vehicle, or cause it to stand, on a road`

#TRACE `s 38A(3) -- after death or sale, pay the balance within one month or the registration is void` 200 28 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 29)
    PARTY `a person driving the vehicle` DOES `drive the vehicle, or cause it to stand, on a road` AT 35
-- expect: BREACH by `a person driving the vehicle`: void registration; s 9(1), maximum penalty $7 500

-- s 40: paying the balance is a permission; not paying breaches nothing.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 40 -- the owner may pay the balance while the registration is in force` 200 180) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 181)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 40 -- the owner may pay the balance while the registration is in force` 200 180) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the registered owner or operator` (`pay the Registrar the balance of the prescribed registration fee` 200) 90)) EQUALS FULFILLED

-- cl 22(3), reg 76(4): the $135 paid on day 10 of the 14 days in the notice.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`Sch 1 cl 22(3), reg 76(4) -- pay the additional licence fee within the time in the Registrar's notice` 135 14) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the licence holder` (`pay the Registrar the additional licence fee` 135) 10)) EQUALS FULFILLED

#TRACE `Sch 1 cl 22(3), reg 76(4) -- pay the additional licence fee within the time in the Registrar's notice` 135 14 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 15)
-- expect: BREACH by `the licence holder`: the fee is recoverable in a court as a debt (reg 76(5))
